Docstring-staleness audit, 2026-09-04, C bundle. Where the A+B+D bundle
(PR #776) removed claims the code no longer supports, these add prose for
functionality that shipped without ever reaching the module docstring. No
claim here is corrected — each is an omission.

  kotlin.py         RECEIVER TYPING (WI-nasuf) was entirely undocumented: the
                    declared-type read, the constructor-typed chain root, the
                    module_hint / receiver_type_hint pair and the ADR-0051
                    reason the slot names the type and not the variable. Also
                    property and enum-entry symbols, extends/implements,
                    decorated_by, references, and the four post-passes.
  ruby.py           Rails/Sinatra routes, ActiveJob-Sidekiq event_publishes,
                    instantiates for .new, field/variable data anchors,
                    included_modules mixins, extends; and the callback set is
                    wider than the three action callbacks named (the _filter
                    spellings, model lifecycle, transaction callbacks, validate).
  cpp.py            Four symbol kinds it emits and did not mention: data-member
                    fields, pure-virtual methods (and the abstract class that
                    follows), enum members, namespace-scope variables; plus
                    references edges for dispatch-table USE.
  ir.py             Edge.confidence_source / rank_score (ADR-0039 rulings 2-3);
                    the provenance group is four fields, not two.
  io_boundary.py    classify_call_in_catalog's io_target_kind discrimination and
                    its qualifier-strip retry.
  gitleaks.py       Three public names, four more safety-zone wrappers, and --
                    the one that matters -- repo_inspect_scan, a SUBPROCESS-zone
                    call that reads the whole analysed repo and so was invisible
                    under a heading called "Filesystem discipline".
  graceful_degrade  RustAnalyzerNotInstalled named; the WI-todon diagnostic layer
                    (once-per-(exc,workspace) dedup, bounded stderr tails, the
                    SIGKILL/OOM shape, the tmp_artifact scratch dir), whose
                    entire purpose is that a silent fall-through and a backend
                    that did nothing look identical.
  rst.py            The docstring-population step; the INV-dulah dual-ID contract.
  migration.py      That it is a ONE-SHOT historical path -- neither input file
                    exists any more -- and that what it still does every run is
                    scaffold stealth/, .gitattributes, .gitignore and config.yaml.
  sync_log.py       write_log always mirrors to stderr, file handle or not.

AND ONE MORE ROTTED CITATION, from this very bundle. Adding lines to cpp.py's
module docstring shifted every line below it, moving MODULE_KEY_NOTIONS'
`disjunction` citation off cpp.py:1393 (now 1404). Re-pointed; 7/7 resolve.

That is the SECOND time today this citation scheme broke, and the more
interesting one: the first (PR #776) came from code movement, this one from a
pure DOCSTRING edit in an unrelated package. EmissionSite stores both `line`
and `anchor`, and the anchor is the real identity -- the line number is a hint
that rots on any edit above it, in any file, for any reason. Filed separately.

Guards: module-docstring first-line check and ruff, both clean.

